{"title":"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/6/fb6804dafc1cf3f0701510be7b725aa3ccde83e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1, S_2, \\ldots, S_{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" /> be finite sets of integers whose intersection is not empty. For each non-empty <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/3/5c3831aa402ffafff3dfaca17ba4b5e02bcab4b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T \\subseteq\\left\\{S_1, S_2, \\ldots, S_{100}\\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"20\" />, the size of the intersection of the sets in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is a multiple of the number of sets in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. What is the least possible number of elements that are in at least 50 sets?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's determine the smallest possible number of elements that appear in at least 50 of the sets.\n</p><p>First, we establish some notation. For any subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/2/d8234cb7d39798469db9343577b7d6d2a38c6c99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T \\subseteq \\{S_1, S_2, \\ldots, S_{100}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"20\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/3/fc3d2d2deb7e3e3dd01261757cf93db92f251f70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cap T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> denote the intersection of all sets in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. By the problem statement, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/a/c5a7b40ffc0661d1b312ac6eca35e78a21a4c4b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\cap T|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"20\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/7/fc73f3216cbfb7ceb707c9c143823d7e5e49f659.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|T|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We'll use a binary encoding approach. For each element <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in our universe, define its \"signature\" as a binary string of length 100, where the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />-th bit is 1 if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/c/3ac9e48d6515ea2a9ffe0ed46fcb9b21ee353ca6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in S_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> and 0 otherwise.\n</p><p>For any signature <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> with exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> ones, corresponding elements must appear in exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> sets. The problem condition requires that for any subset of sets corresponding to positions where 1's appear in some signature <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, the number of elements having signature <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> that contains all 1's from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/9/fd97769233c650a7cf8c92093d6c50a7708157ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|u|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"22\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Let's denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/5/325c0305af875b35a752925de130f0e336d8b965.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(v)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"20\" /> the number of elements with signature <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. The problem condition translates to: for any signature <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/9/fd97769233c650a7cf8c92093d6c50a7708157ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|u|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"22\" height=\"20\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/c/a6c3e88c8660f6f91221e8401237fcdd38733a57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{v \\supseteq u} f(v)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"65\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Key claim: For any signature <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/b/8fbaf86d6a43f1f0311f24cbd6e7db4d4e97339a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|u| = 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" />, we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/8/36894e5a810241483a34f1eb2eba343ccb6d10c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(u) \\geq 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Proof: By the divisibility condition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/c/a6c3e88c8660f6f91221e8401237fcdd38733a57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{v \\supseteq u} f(v)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"65\" height=\"45\" /> must be divisible by 50. For any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> strictly containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, if we sum over all such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> of size 50, each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/5/325c0305af875b35a752925de130f0e336d8b965.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(v)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"20\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/7/1f7036715d00220d91f8ffa6277606db2528178f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|v| &gt; 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" /> gets counted multiple times. To satisfy the divisibility condition for each individual <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/8/36894e5a810241483a34f1eb2eba343ccb6d10c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(u) \\geq 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" /> for each signature <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> with exactly 50 ones.\n</p><p>Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/6/f56bfcb688995c70e172c402301bfb09245fe32f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{100}{50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"57\" height=\"55\" /> different ways to choose 50 positions for ones in the signature, and each such signature must correspond to at least 50 elements, the minimum number of elements appearing in at least 50 sets is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/1/f711357a37970e9bdfdea44566127253b32c1a42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50 \\binom{100}{50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"75\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/4/d24f23349e57b978f85bf649609ee86d52650daa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{50 \\binom{100}{50}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -29px\" width=\"87\" height=\"67\" />.\n</p><p>~ brandonyee\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> be the intersection set of all elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, that is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/0/b406d80cebbe95f4fa2556bbbf8f1b30479dc877.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k = \\bigcap_{\\text{all elements}} T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"128\" height=\"43\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/c/8cca296857f16ef0956f831b21c1c6103ccd4958.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_k|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"20\" /> is the size of the intersection set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/7/fc73f3216cbfb7ceb707c9c143823d7e5e49f659.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|T|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> is the number of elements, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94bb13e8aad32352e8bf542f96e2b316245164af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_k| = |T|m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" /> for an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. Consider the conditional operator <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/3/203b23e7f9ca3fbe042bd46deef03758b1c2a8fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{1}: \\ \\{x \\} \\rightarrow \\{0,1 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"20\" /> if in or not in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e0ec34cd8860ceb97113f81ba768ba739ad5166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Then, define an <i>encoded sequence</i> to be a string of 100 consisting of some number of 1's and 0's. \n</p><p><b>Lemma:</b> The number of viable <b>encoded sequences</b> is bijective to the problem statement.\n</p><p>By the statement, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> denotes the <i>encoded sequence</i>, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd8440785b5045b1a3e91e4991372220a5c90171.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(x) = (\\{\\}_{k=1}^{100} \\mathbf{1}_{x \\in S_k}) \\in \\{0,1 \\}^{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"253\" height=\"21\" />. Define the <i>support</i> sequence to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd91ede540a63d380787dc845d37d99a8c24eb38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{supp}(E) = \\{S_i \\ : \\ x \\in S_i \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"203\" height=\"20\" />. By convention the correspondence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/2/a82e9ae54d0192800b39090b5c2d5c8797564bb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\mapsto E(x) \\mapsto \\operatorname{supp}(E(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"198\" height=\"20\" />. We just need to prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7cc53e4989ce5132139e0871bd7f7f9d22d67131.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{supp}(E(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" /> contains the same number of elements as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Luckily, this correspondence already situates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/c/2ac4e263fd8dd81603d6d0dbb8365a9d6a7d68da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{i \\ : \\ \\mathbf{1}_{x \\in S_i}  \\iff \\operatorname{supp}(E(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"229\" height=\"20\" />. By definition then the number of ones in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/3/9d32e8ac75bf3a4a7441aadee07de329926e1508.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> is equivalent to the size of the support of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/3/9d32e8ac75bf3a4a7441aadee07de329926e1508.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />. Thus, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is our support set, the bijection is developed, that is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/8/c98952c0d22445e09151c06aacdfc508f0571b4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{1}(E(x)) = |T|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>The last part is to expand this to what we defined an encoded sequence to be, particularly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/1/ac10f1eb6ca6b0a4340d127c8115af87136e1764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in \\bigcap_{S_i \\in T} S_i  \\iff T \\subseteq \\operatorname{supp}(E(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"268\" height=\"45\" /> by the definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. However, we established that because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/9/6a94858c1cee7fc8e643da30d8ee419eaed7de6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{1}(E(x))= |\\operatorname{supp}(E(x))| = |T|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"241\" height=\"20\" />, it is given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/9/7a966a77f4f5f7fef8f872c4054b6d40140d55be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T= \\operatorname{supp}(E(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" />, which is what we desired. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><b>2024 USAMO P2:</b>\n</p><p>In the encoded sequence, we choose 50 to be 1 and the rest 0, in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/6/f56bfcb688995c70e172c402301bfb09245fe32f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{100}{50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"57\" height=\"55\" /> ways.\n</p><p>At this minimality,  all elements of this set share the support set that contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/d/04d0ac9cadf1239a75ce5ed80e86d974482100e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum \\mathbf{1}(x) = 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"108\" height=\"31\" />. Thus the minimum number of elements in every given passage is 50, yielding the minimalist value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/1/f711357a37970e9bdfdea44566127253b32c1a42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50 \\binom{100}{50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"75\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p><p>By <b>Lemma</b>, there is a bijection, and thus, the count is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/5/6b55458c66b246803a6db438b83599d1abce08a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{50 \\binom{100}{50}} \\qquad \\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -29px\" width=\"134\" height=\"67\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p><p><b>Remark:</b> \n</p><p>Solution 1 contains much handwaving and cannot be deemed a proper proof, which is why I created this.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/eguz1OuckH0\">https://youtu.be/eguz1OuckH0</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO\" title=\"2024 USAMO\">2024 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2024\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017163746\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.042 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.109 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 404/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1313/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 13080/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.881      1 -total\n 56.14%    7.232      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 42.10%    5.423      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:27286:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017163746 and rev